Fix this async race so count reliably prints 3. Serialize increments with a mutex/lock/queue:
```ts
let count = 0;
async function increment() {
  const current = count;
  await Promise.resolve();
  count = current + 1;
}
await Promise.all([increment(), increment(), increment()]);
console.log(count);
```
